  "notes": [
    "Default domains are a coverage plan, not claims of ISA support or reachability.",
    "C2 trap events without mode retain mode=unknown; mode is not inferred.",
    "RVFI intr marks trap-handler entry, including synchronous traps; actual interrupt causes use C2 trap events.",
    "retired counts C2 instruction records, including trap=true records.",
    "CSR/mnemonic groups without declared bins report observations, not a completeness percentage.",
    "rd_x0 records RVFI rd=0, which also denotes instructions without a destination.",
    "dependency: an FP destination is the instruction encoding's rd (C2 rd is the integer write); when the trace reports an integer rd for an FP-destination instruction, the next instruction's back_to_back is undetermined.",
    "Memory alignment uses each trace's platform address convention (aligned_mem: mem_addr plus the mask's lane offset); a lane-shifted mask under an unknown or byte convention is undetermined."
